('003', 'Active', 'SomeOtherCounty', 'District C', 'http://school3.example.com', 1, '2023-01-03', 'DOE', 'P', '2023-10-03');

-- Both Q1 and Q2 will return the websites for CDSCode '001' and '002'.

-- If one were to try to force a difference one would have to introduce an expression with side effects (for example a UDF that behaves differently when evaluated first or second). Without such non–traditional behavior (which is not recommended and is not part of the given schema), no counterexample exists.

