/*
Example of the danger in an outer-context:

SELECT A.atom_id, A.element, 
       (SELECT T.element FROM ATOM AS T WHERE T.atom_id = 'TR000_1') AS q1,
       (SELECT element FROM ATOM WHERE atom_id = 'TR000_1') AS q2
FROM ATOM A
WHERE A.atom_id = 'TR000_2';

Here, the outer query (alias A) already has an "element" column (with value 'He').
When the unqualified reference in Q2 is resolved, some SQL implementations may bind it to the outer A.element, so that q2 returns 'He' rather than the intended inner row's element 'H'.  On the other hand, Q1 explicitly qualifies the column, so q1 returns 'H'.
*/

