Q2 is:
  SELECT T1.Name
  FROM BADGES AS T1
  INNER JOIN USERS AS T2 ON T1.UserId = T2.Id
  WHERE T2.DisplayName = 'Pierre'
If the DBMS resolves the ambiguous column reference T1.Name in a way that (say) prefers the USERS column when available (or due to a mis‐configuration), then Q2 would return 'UserPierre' rather than 'BadgeAward'.
*/

