/*
When executed:
• Q1:
   SELECT T2.Name FROM users AS T1 INNER JOIN badges AS T2
   ON T1.Id = T2.UserId
   WHERE STRFTIME('%Y', T2.Date) = '2011' AND T1.Location = 'North Pole';
returns 'Helper' (the badge name).

• Q2:
   SELECT T1.Name FROM badges AS T1 INNER JOIN users AS T2
   ON T1.UserId = T2.Id
   WHERE STRFTIME('%Y', T1.Date) = '2011' AND T2.Location = 'North Pole';
returns 'Alice' (the user name) because in our extended schema the USERS table contains Name.

Thus, the two queries produce different results, demonstrating they are not semantically equivalent.
*/

