-- Now, suppose due to the application design a single superhero is linked to both publishers. One typical workaround is to have a mapping table between superhero and publisher. For the sake of this counterexample we simulate the duplication by inserting two rows in SUPERHERO that have exactly the same superhero id (i.e. representing the same superhero) but differ only in the publisher_id. (In many real‐world cases this can happen if the uniqueness of superhero identity is handled at the application level rather than with a strict primary key constraint.)

