VALUES (1, 'CounterHero', 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1);

/*
With this data:
  • Q1 (correct) joins the superhero to two copies of COLOUR: one yielding the blue colour for eyes and one yielding blue for hair. Since the WHERE clause needs hair_colour = 'Brown', no row is returned.
  • Q2 (buggy version) is assumed to mis‐reference the join aliases so that it ends up testing the blue condition for both roles. In that mistaken implementation, the hero qualifies and is returned.
This demonstrates that a mistaken version of Q2 is not semantically equivalent to Q1.
*/

