/*
Intended queries:
Q1: SELECT name, date FROM races WHERE year = 1999 ORDER BY round DESC LIMIT 1;
   --> Returns: 'Race 2' (since round 2 is the highest)

Q2: SELECT name, date FROM races WHERE year = 1999 ORDER BY round ASC LIMIT 1;
   --> Returns: 'Race 1' (since round 1 is the lowest)

This counterexample demonstrates that if one query orders by descending and the other by ascending round, their results diverge.
*/

