-- Q1 (which starts with Patient as T1) will return two rows (one for each Patient row joined with the one Laboratory record),
-- whereas Q2 (which starts from Laboratory as T1) will return one row for ID=1 because that Laboratory row joins with the set of Patient rows but the driving set is Laboratory.
-- (Under bag semantics the duplicate‐multiplicities might “leak” differently even though the final set is the same if duplicates are removed.)

